- a partial card refund booked once as the hand-back, with a balanced debit-1110 / credit-1030 entry, A's tenant and accounts, nothing in B, the ticket still cancelled, no fiscal document, and an audit entry naming the card-machine refund;
- a rejected ticket;
- too much refused before the machine is asked (more than the card payment; more than is still owed after a hand-back recorded by hand);
- a card-machine refund in progress blocks both the record-only hand-back and a second card-machine refund;
- a concurrent double click, with the same key and with new keys, refunds once;
- booking the same card-machine refund twice returns the first row;
- company B gets 404 and a cashier gets 403, and B's own ticket books only in B;
- an open ticket is still NOT_REFUNDABLE;
- the admin offer helper, run against real server answers, matches the server: its maximum is accepted and one paisa more is refused.

